1
00:00:00,274 --> 00:00:02,322
Are Zeus and Jupiter the same god?

2
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:03,785
In myth, yes.

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,182
In Rome, no.

4
00:00:05,553 --> 00:00:07,444
Ovid tells the stories of Zeus under

5
00:00:07,254 --> 00:00:08,168
Latin names:

6
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:10,532
the son of Saturn, the thunderbolt controller.

7
00:00:10,877 --> 00:00:13,808
Birth, thunderbolt, kingship, love affairs:

8
00:00:13,881 --> 00:00:15,982
it's Hesiod and Homer in Roman dress.

9
00:00:16,366 --> 00:00:18,131
And the name only travels one way:

10
00:00:18,204 --> 00:00:20,316
Greek texts never call Zeus Jupiter.

11
00:00:20,654 --> 00:00:22,703
But in cult, he's a different god.

12
00:00:22,827 --> 00:00:24,487
Rome's first temple was his:

13
00:00:24,529 --> 00:00:27,355
Jupiter Feretrius, where Romulus hung the spoils

14
00:00:27,165 --> 00:00:28,310
of the king he killed.

15
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:30,994
As his army flees, Romulus vows him

16
00:00:30,805 --> 00:00:31,719
another temple:

17
00:00:31,792 --> 00:00:33,536
Jupiter Stator, the Stayer.

18
00:00:33,922 --> 00:00:36,264
And in Virgil, Jupiter promises Rome an

19
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:37,451
empire without end.

20
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:40,067
Hesiod's Zeus rules because the gods asked

21
00:00:39,878 --> 00:00:40,519
him to.

22
00:00:40,647 --> 00:00:42,643
And he promises no city anything.

23
00:00:43,013 --> 00:00:43,906
Rule of thumb:

24
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,154
in the stories, Jupiter is the Roman

25
00:00:45,964 --> 00:00:46,616
Zeus.

26
00:00:46,723 --> 00:00:48,761
In religion, he's the god of Rome.

27
00:00:49,129 --> 00:00:50,526
Which text says so?

28
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,871
Ovid and Hesiod for the myth; Livy

29
00:00:52,681 --> 00:00:53,953
and Virgil for Rome.

30
00:00:54,319 --> 00:00:56,179
Save it, and send it to anyone

31
00:00:55,989 --> 00:00:57,838
who says Jupiter is just Zeus with

32
00:00:57,649 --> 00:00:58,427
a new name.

